  "text_input": "52-year-old male with known Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and Systemic Hypertension for 15 years presented with scrotal swelling and bilateral lower limb swelling since 4 days. No history of cough, breathlessness, pain abdomen, or trauma. Diagnosed with Diabetic Kidney Disease with anasarca including scrotal and prepuceal edema, NPDR, and hypertensive retinopathy. USG showed hepatomegaly with Grade 1 fatty changes and bilateral moderate pleural effusion. Urine showed significant proteinuria and hematuria. Serum albumin critically low at 2.3 g/dL. Vibration sense lost up to ASIS on left lower limb consistent with peripheral neuropathy.",
